<article class="env-lemma" id="01PC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01PC">Lemma <span data-tag="01PC">28.17.2</span>.</a> Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ be an affine scheme. The quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules $\widetilde M$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation if and only if $M$ is an $R$-module of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $\widetilde M$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01PB" data-tag="01PB">28.17.1</a> we see that $M$ is a finite $R$-module. Choose a surjection $R^ n \to M$ with kernel $K$. By Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01HV" data-tag="01HV">26.5.4</a> there is a short exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \widetilde{K} \to \bigoplus \mathcal{O}_ X^{\oplus n} \to \widetilde{M} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01BP" data-tag="01BP">17.11.4</a> we see that $\widetilde{K}$ is a finite type $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/01PB" data-tag="01PB">28.17.1</a> again we see that $K$ is a finite $R$-module. Hence $M$ is an $R$-module of finite presentation. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>